#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= Air Travel Guidelines

== Commercial Airline Bookings

Air travel represents a substantial corporate investment. Employees must select standard non-refundable fares through approved corporate travel management tools.

#policy-rule("POL-AIR-001", "Economy Class Standard")[
  Economy class is mandatory for all domestic flights and short-haul international flights where scheduled flight duration is under eight (8) consecutive hours. Premium Economy is permissible for flights between six (6) and eight (8) hours if approved by a Director.
]

#policy-rule("POL-AIR-002", "Business Class Long-Haul Exception")[
  Business class travel is permitted exclusively for non-stop scheduled flights exceeding eight (8) continuous hours duration, or where an employee is expected to conduct critical client meetings within four (4) hours of arrival. First Class travel is strictly prohibited across all routes.
]

== Advance Booking Requirements

Airfares escalate rapidly as departure dates approach. Employees are required to plan travel well in advance.

#policy-rule("POL-AIR-003", "Fourteen-Day Advance Booking")[
  Airline reservations must be completed at least fourteen (14) calendar days prior to domestic departure and twenty-one (21) days prior to international departure. Bookings made inside these windows require written manager justification for short-notice travel.
]

== Ancillary Airline Fees

Airlines frequently levy supplemental charges for luggage, seating, and boarding priorities.

#policy-warning("POL-AIR-004", "Baggage and Seat Selection Restrictions")[
  The company reimburses one (1) standard checked baggage fee per traveler. Fees for preferred seat selection, extra legroom, priority boarding, airport lounge access, and onboard Wi-Fi for personal non-emergency use are non-reimbursable.
]
